# .gcloudignore — controls what `gcloud run jobs deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
# When this file exists, gcloud uses it INSTEAD of falling back to .gitignore.
#
# Strategy: allowlist. Ignore everything at the repo root, then re-include only the
# files Buildpacks needs to build the container. This guarantees secrets (.env),
# Terraform state, and local caches can never leak into the build context — including
# files added to the repo later.
#
# If you add a new build input (e.g. another package dir), re-include it below.

# Ignore everything at the top level...
/*

# ...except the inputs the Python (uv) buildpack needs:
!/src
!/config
!/pyproject.toml
!/uv.lock
!/Procfile

# Strip Python caches that may live inside the re-included dirs:
src/**/__pycache__/
config/**/__pycache__/
